Groupe 3R confirmed that administrative data including employee personal information was stolen and internal documents published, so exfiltration is no longer only Akira's claim; whether patient medical data was taken cannot be established. Its 20 centres span seven cantons including Zurich, the 2025 attack stole data without disrupting operations, and Groupe 3R attributes the 2026 attack to Akira on the basis of methods its partners observed rather than a forensic finding. No source states the access vector, so the edge-device playbook and the generic actions give way to the operator's fraud warning.
